---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-11-20';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Wyreup"
  description="How Wyreup handles local file processing, public domain registration lookups and platform data."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <header>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Local file tools process on your device.</strong> Network lookups explain
      what they send before you run them. We use no analytics or tracking cookies.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>You decide what gets sent.</strong> You choose which
      tools to invoke and which inputs to submit. You are responsible
      for confirming you have the right to submit the input and for
      whatever you do with the output. See section 3 of the
      <a href="/legal/terms">Terms of Service</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What we collect</h2>

    <h3>Local tools and free public lookups</h3>
    <p>Local file tools keep their file processing on your device. Setup
      downloads and cached assets depend on the tool.</p>
    <p>The free Domain Registration Age lookup sends the entered domain
      to Wyreup. Wyreup reads the fixed public IANA bootstrap without
      sending IANA the queried domain, then sends the domain to its
      registration registry. No API key is required. Registration age
      may describe the current registration rather than first-ever use.
      Wyreup returns only minimized registration dates, ages, status,
      and source information, without registrant contact details.</p>
    <p>Public lookup admission stores temporary rotating HMAC network
      counters and random short-lived reservation tokens in our existing
      database. Counter digests rotate each database minute; tokens are
      random invocation reservations with a 30-second expiry. There is
      no raw IP or domain-query database for these lookups. The trusted
      connection IP is used transiently to calculate the counter digest.
      Shared networks can reach the six-admissions-per-minute network
      limit together. Global admission is limited to 60 per minute and
      eight outstanding reservations; minute boundaries can admit two
      adjacent windows' allowances. These limits do not guarantee fair
      scheduling or immunity to overload.</p>
    <p>Expired counters and tokens are pruned on later valid requests,
      not by a guaranteed physical deletion timer. Platform logs and
      backups have their own retention. No domain-query history or new
      analytics is added by this lookup. Local shell history, MCP audit
      metadata, assistant-provider records, saved chains, output files,
      and operator exports can retain requests or results independently.
      The lookup does not erase those records.</p>

    <h2>Service providers and model downloads</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare provides site hosting, Pages Functions and the D1 database for
      public-lookup admission. See Cloudflare's
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy policy</a>.
      Some local tools download code, codecs or model files from asset hosts before
      processing. Those requests can expose standard connection information to the
      asset host. The local tool processes your input on your device.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Email <strong>hello@wyreup.com</strong> with requests to access, correct,
      export or delete personal data we hold about you.</p>
    <p>
      If you are in the EU/UK, you also have the right to lodge a
      complaint with your local supervisory authority.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Wyreup is not directed at children under 13 (or under 16 in the EU).
      We do not knowingly collect their information.
    </p>

    <h2>Data transfers and edge routing</h2>
    <p>
      Wyreup is operated from Indiana, United States. Domain Registration Age
      lookups pass through Cloudflare's global network to the public registration
      registry shown in the result. Requests can cross borders, and Wyreup does
      not control the country a request passes through. Review the lookup
      destination and the rules that apply to your data before you submit it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We show the date of the latest revision at the top of this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions or rights requests: <strong>hello@wyreup.com</strong>.<br />
      Security disclosures: <strong>security@wyreup.com</strong>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-6) var(--space-4) var(--space-12);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    color: var(--text-primary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl, 28px);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-2);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal ul {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: var(--space-5);
  }
  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .legal code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.92em;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    padding: 1px 4px;
  }
  .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
</style>
